.TH COF-RUN-LIBRARY 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-run-library \- Fetch and run a shared library orchestration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof run-library [OPTIONS] {asset_id}
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetches a shared library orchestration and runs it in one step -- the same
fetch cof fetch does, followed by the same execution cof run does.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B asset_id
ASSET_ID Shared library asset identifier.
.TP
.B --version, -V
VERSION Specific asset version. Defaults to latest.
.TP
.B --config, -c
CONFIG Path to config JSON (or use CIRCUITRY_CONFIG).
.TP
.B --auth-token
AUTH_TOKEN Shared library auth token (or set CIRCUITRY_LIBRARY_TOKEN).
.TP
.B --service-profile
SERVICE_PROFILE Apply runtime overrides from
runtime.library.service_profiles.<name>.
.TP
.B --state, -s
STATE Optional input state JSON.
.TP
.B --out, -o
OUT Write resulting state JSON to this path.
.TP
.B --pretty
Pretty-print JSON when writing/printing.
.TP
.B --print
Print resulting state JSON to stdout.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Skip adapter calls; validate/plan only.
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable output only (minimal logs).
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress non-essential output.
.TP
.B --verbose, -v
Show detailed progress.
.TP
.B --live-state
LIVE_STATE Mirror state atomically to this file while the run goes (at most
every 0.5 s, and once more when it ends). For live monitoring.
.TP
.B --events
EVENTS Write a JSONL stream of effect starts and ends to this file as the run
goes (created or truncated up front). Shows what --live-state cannot: a
running tree branch, use child, or chain leaf.
.TP
.B -e
ENV_VARS Inline state variable (KEY=VALUE). Repeatable.
.TP
.B --tail
Print only the final effect's value as plain text. Ideal for piping.
.TP
.B --skip-preflight
Bypass dependency preflight; run even if check()s reported missing deps.
.TP
.B --allow-capabilities
ALLOW_CAPABILITIES Comma-separated capabilities
(shell,python_eval,fs-write,network) to approve for this run without prompting
— a scripted/CI escape hatch. Not persisted; see `cof trust` to approve a
document permanently.
.TP
.B --profile
PROFILE Named profile to apply (profiles/<name>.yml, orchestration-scoped wins
over project-level). Precedence: CLI > profile > orchestration > config.
.TP
.B --adapter
ADAPTER Adapter to use for this run. Beats CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER and the
orchestration.
.TP
.B --model
MODEL Model to use for this run. Beats CIRCUITRY_MODEL and the orchestration.
.TP
.B --explain-routing
Print each prompt effect's complexity score, band, and model choice as it
dispatches. Needs runtime.complexity.scoring.enabled; prints nothing if
scoring is off. Suppressed by --quiet/--json.
.TP
.B --scoring, --no-scoring
Force runtime.complexity.scoring on/off for this run. Beats --profile and the
orchestration/config; omit to leave it resolved as configured.
.TP
.B --routing, --no-routing
Force runtime.complexity.routing on/off for this run. Beats --profile and the
orchestration/config; --no-routing also drops any profile per-effect routing
pin, since routing is off for the whole run either way. Requires scoring (from
this flag or config) when turned on.
.TP
.B --decompose, --no-decompose
Force runtime.complexity.decomposition on/off for this run. Beats --profile
and the orchestration/config. Requires scoring (from this flag or config) when
turned on.
.TP
.B --split, --no-split
Force runtime.complexity.splitting on/off for this run. Beats --profile and
the orchestration/config. Needs no scoring: an effect's own
split.budget_tokens still splits even with this off, and --no-split does not
stop it either — only an effect's own split.enabled: false opts it out.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
An explicit config JSON path. Checked before a trusted project config in the
current directory and the global config; replaces both rather than layering on
top of them.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_MODEL
Overrides the resolved config's default_model.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER
Overrides the resolved config's default_adapter.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER_URL
Overrides the resolved default adapter's own base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_COMFYUI_URL
Overrides the comfyui plugin's own base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_SYSTEMONE_URL
Overrides the systemone plugin's own base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_ADAPTERS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_adapters.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_PLUGINS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_plugins.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_TOOLS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_tools.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENVIRONMENT
Overrides the resolved config's environment (dev, prod, or test).
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_TRUST_PROJECT_CONFIG
Trusts a project config in the current directory without running cof trust
first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/config.json
The global config, the last layer config resolution tries.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/.env
Private environment variables, loaded before config resolution (written by cof
setup).
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Project configs trusted by cof trust; config resolution consults it before
applying a discovered project config.
.TP
.I ./circuitry.config.json, ./config.json
A project config in the working directory, applied only once trusted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-fetch(1)\fR, \fBcof-run(1)\fR, \fBcof-library(1)\fR
